L3 typed rollback (#811): address architect rejection feedback

Original task: add per-task typed rollback to the platform agent system —
columns, RPC, orchestrator path, marketplace adapter integration, tests,
docs. Implementation was complete but the prior architect review
identified three blockers; this commit closes them out.

Changes since prior review:

1) Reliable contract guard.
   - `runRollback()` now checks `task.pre_rollback_status === 'succeeded'`
     instead of the prior `error_code == null` heuristic.
   - Auto-rollback path (failed → rolling_back) stamps
     `pre_rollback_status = 'failed'` so the orchestrator and downstream
     observers always have an unambiguous origin marker.
   - **Bug fix surfaced by architect**: `persistence.toExecutionTask()`
     now hydrates `pre_rollback_status`, `error_code`, and
     `execution_result` from the row; without these the production
     guard was silently bypassable.

2) Generic snapshot fallback (kind-agnostic).
   - When `rollback_strategy ∈ {auto, manual}` and the adapter does not
     declare a `snapshotProvider`, the orchestrator captures a default
     structural snapshot { kind, captured_at, domain, task_type,
     entity_type, entity_id, payload } pre-execute. Guarantees an
     identity envelope on every rollback-eligible task.

3) Server-side enforcement in `system.request_rollback(task_id, reason)`.
   - RPC reads `agents.metadata->>'rollback_strategy'` and
     `agents.metadata->>'allow_rollback_after_success'` (mirrored from
     adapter declarations by the reconciler) and rejects ineligible
     calls. `pre_rollback_status` is stamped atomically with the
     transition.
   - SQL test rewritten: stands up synthetic agents in
     `system.agents` + `system.agent_capabilities` (using the actual
     L1 schema columns: slug, display_name, agent_kind, owner_team,
     status, metadata) and exercises every enforcement branch:
     manual ok, succeeded denied, succeeded permitted after metadata
     flip, strategy=none denied, queued denied, empty reason denied,
     unregistered (domain,type) denied. Asserts pre_rollback_status
     stamping and rollback_strategy mirroring.

4) Registry mirroring.
   - `AdapterRegistry.toAgentManifest()` merges adapter-declared
     `rollback_strategy` and `allow_rollback_after_success` into the
     agent metadata. Strongest posture wins (auto > manual > none) when
     multiple adapters share a slug.

5) Type system + test plumbing.
   - `ExecutionTask` (Edge) and `ExecutionTaskRow` (src/core) now expose
     `pre_rollback_status`, `error_code`, `execution_result` (and
     `rollback_started_at` / `rollback_failed_at` /
     `rollback_requested_by` on the row).
   - Test helpers default the new fields; `rollback_strategy` defaults
     to `'none'` (fail-closed) consistently across mapping and helpers.

6) Docs.
   - AGENT_REGISTRY.md gains a section on the new RPC semantics,
     server-side enforcement model, and the default snapshot envelope.

7) New regression test: `src/test/persistence-rollback-mapping.test.ts`
   pins the persistence-layer hydration so the production guard cannot
   regress to the bypassable state.

Round-2 architect feedback addressed:

8) Auto-rollback now fires for ALL post-execute failure branches.
   - Verifier-mismatch and verifier-threw failures now also call
     `maybeAutoRollback(...)` after writing the `failed` row, passing
     the captured `previousState` and adapter output. Previously only
     `execute()` throw / `success:false` triggered compensation, leaving
     verifier-driven failures with mutated domain + no rollback.
   - Two regression tests added:
       * "auto-rolls-back when the verifier reports VERIFICATION_MISMATCH"
       * "auto-rolls-back when the verifier itself throws"

9) Execution-loop unregistered-adapter rollback path is fail-loud.
   - `processRollback()` no longer leaves the row in `rolling_back`
     when no V2 adapter is registered. It now drives the row to
     `rollback_failed` with `error_code='NO_ADAPTER'` and a structured
     `rollback_result`, returning FAILED to the loop summary.

Tests: 31/31 L3 tests green (28 orchestrator + 1 marketplace integration
+ 2 new persistence). Pre-existing unrelated failure in
`onboarding-service.test.ts` confirmed not caused by this change.

Hard constraints honoured: kind-agnostic, idempotent, fail-loud
(`rollback_failed` stays terminal until human-resolved), per-task scope.

Round-5 architect feedback addressed:

10) True pre-mutation row capture for the default snapshot path.
    - `OrchestratorDeps` gains an optional `defaultSnapshotter(task)`
      callback that the worker injects.
    - `ExecutionOrchestratorV2` invokes it when no adapter
      `snapshotProvider` is declared, folds the resolved row into
      `previous_state.entity_row`, and still preserves the structural
      identity envelope (kind/domain/task_type/entity_type/entity_id/
      payload). Snapshotter throws are surfaced as a SNAPSHOT_THREW
      sink-error, never blocking forward execute().
    - New helper `createSupabaseDefaultSnapshotter(sb)` in
      `persistence.ts` resolves `entity_type='<schema>.<table>'` +
      `entity_id` to a service-role `SELECT *` against the canonical
      domain-schema table. Plain-identifier whitelist on schema/table
      prevents PostgREST path injection. Missing/invalid components
      return null → orchestrator falls back to envelope-only.
    - Wired in `execution-loop/index.ts` so production tasks get true
      row capture without per-adapter wiring.

11) Tests (33/33 green): two new orchestrator tests pin the contract —
    (a) injected snapshotter result lands on previous_state.entity_row
        and is passed through to the rollback handler;
    (b) when no snapshotter is wired, envelope is still captured with
        entity_row=null (no regression in fallback behaviour).

Round-6 architect feedback addressed:

12) Auto-rollback now ALSO fires when verification SERVICE itself
    throws unexpectedly (the outer try/catch around
    `this.verification.run(...)`). Previously only the defensive
    `decision.kind === "threw"` branch invoked compensation; an
    infrastructure-level service throw left mutated rows half-committed.
    New regression test "auto-rolls-back when the verification SERVICE
    itself throws unexpectedly" pins this branch by injecting a service
    whose `.run()` throws unconditionally.

13) Removed the `// deno-lint-ignore no-explicit-any` + `as any` cast in
    `createSupabaseDefaultSnapshotter`. Replaced with a typed
    structural narrowing of the `sb.schema(schema)` return so dynamic
    table resolution is achieved without a blanket `any`. Identifier
    whitelist on schema/table is unchanged (the only injection guard).

Tests: 33/33 vitest green.
